// Phase 08 Task 1 -- Pattern B (UsesParam), "ACCEPTING" member in name only.
//
// OBSERVED VERDICT (as of Phase 10 plan 10-06, PHASE-10-DEBT.md D-10-27/
// D-10-28/D-10-29): this fixture is refused, IDENTICALLY to twin_b_refuse.schway,
// with `check.interprocedural_loan_liveness`. The intended split (this member
// admitted, the refusing member refused) does NOT materialize, and per D-10-27
// that is NOT a `deriveFunctionUsesParam` defect to fix in Phase 10 -- six
// independently-authored, currently-passing Phase 08/09 tests pin the current
// derivation semantics as intended, and applying the narrowing D-09-53
// proposed was re-executed and found to break them, including this fixture's
// own test.
//
// WHY: probe's body (`taken = take buffer; taken`) is a ONE-HOP identity
// forward, not the zero-hop direct return `deriveFunctionUsesParam`'s OpReturn
// exemption actually covers (check.go's doc comment, corrected alongside this
// header) -- the intermediate `take` (OpMove) trips the default arm and sets
// `usesParam = true` before the scan ever reaches the OpReturn. So `check`
// itself, correctly per its own contract, derives probe's `usesParam` as true.
//
// The REAL gap, re-filed as D-10-28 rather than re-pointing D-09-53: even a
// callee that genuinely never uses its parameter (usesParam == false) could
// not demonstrate Pattern B's split end to end here, because `corevalidate`
// has NO `usesParam` peer at all (`corevalidate_peer_liveness.go`'s
// `peerLoanCarryFact` carries only `ReturnsBorrowOfParam`, Pattern A's fact).
// `corevalidate`'s own liveness walk treats every OpCall argument
// unconditionally as a use, so it refuses escort's call to probe regardless
// of what `check` derives -- a missing second detector, not a broken existing
// one. D-10-28's landing phase is open (Phase 11 or M003 are candidate homes).
//
// See twin_b_refuse.schway's header for the full, load-bearing explanation of
// why the real ast.Program -> check.Program pipeline cannot observe a
// contract-driven difference end to end for either member of this pair: the
// caller's own `borrow; move; call` shape is refused INTRAPROCEDURALLY
// (ownership.move_while_borrowed) for BOTH members alike, before the
// interprocedural pass this plan's fixtures exist to exercise ever runs --
// computeLoanLastUses' AST-shadow path is summary-blind by construction
// (08-02's own documented finding), not a defect newly introduced here.

module phase08.twin_b_accept

export {
  fn escort
}

fn probe(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let taken = take buffer
  taken
}

fn escort(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let delivered = take buffer
  let observed = probe(borrowed)
  observed
}
